course: dictionary
lesson: 5497
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Lavender is one of them. It can be a plant, a pale purple colour or a sweet scent. «Badger shows them to a room half full of apples, potatoes, nuts and honey, with two little white beds smelling of lavender.» Here the beds smell of lavender, so lavender means the sweet scent.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. The words around lavender are the clues. «The beds are clean and smell beautifully of lavender.» The word beautifully tells you the smell is pleasant, so lavender is the sweet-smelling scent made from the flowers.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you think lavender is a colour, does «the beds smell beautifully of a pale purple» make sense? It does not, so the colour meaning is wrong here. Swapping in a meaning is a quick check you can use every time.
fact: Lavender is a small bush with sweet-smelling purple flowers.
fact: Lavender can also mean a pale purple colour.
fact: Lavender is the oil or scent made from the flowers, used in soaps and perfumes.
fact: «The beds are clean and smell beautifully of lavender» uses lavender to mean the sweet scent.
fact: Bees love lavender flowers, so you may find them buzzing around a lavender bush in summer.
exercise: «The beds are clean and smell beautifully of lavender.» What does lavender mean here? | *A sweet, flowery smell | A loud noise | A cold wind
exercise: Mia painted her bedroom wall lavender. What colour is the wall? | *Pale purple | Bright red | Dark brown | Deep green
exercise: Which of these is a lavender plant? | A stone wall | *A small bush with purple flowers | A type of fish | A tall tree with green leaves
test: Dad put lavender bags in the drawer so the clothes smell nice. What is the lavender? | A kind of wooden box | *Dried flowers with a sweet smell | Wet paint | A loud bell
test: Ella says lavender in «a lavender dress» is a plant. What is the right meaning here? | A sweet scent | *A pale purple colour | A small bush | A tiny bird
exam: Jo says lavender can be a plant, a colour or a scent. How can you tell which meaning is right? | Lavender is always a colour, so always pick colour | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Ask a bee | Pick the longest meaning
